                "Mainframe > Resources, at the bottom of the main page, opens a panel under the Mainframe with your CPU, RAM and GPU right now. In each bar Capri's share is cyan and everything else is red. CAPRI lists her own parts, like the app itself, her brain (llama-server) and HD voice (tts-server), and OTHER PROGRAMS lists what else uses the most, grouped by name. RAM is each program's private memory, like Task Manager shows. GPU needs Windows' GPU counters. Her built-in brain stops after 5 minutes unused, or 30 seconds after you pick another brain, and starts again when she needs it.", "MainframeSystem.cs", "Resources"),
            new Topic("Brain VRAM", "brain vram|vram limit|limit vram|limit your vram|your vram|use less vram|vram usage|uses too much vram|graphics memory|gpu memory|offload to ram|offload to cpu|cpu offload|cpu offloading|split vram and ram|run your brain in ram|brain on the cpu",
                "Mainframe > Resources > Brain VRAM sets the most graphics card memory her built-in brain or an Ollama model takes: Auto, 8 GB, 6 GB, 4 GB, 3 GB, 2 GB or RAM only. Auto lets it take what fits, like before. With a limit the part of the model that doesn't fit runs from RAM on the CPU, so her replies come slower but games keep more of the card and more FPS. That also lets a bigger, smarter Ollama model run on a small card when there's RAM to spare. Her built-in brain loads again with the new limit at once; Ollama picks it up on the next message. It leaves cloud brains and other local servers like LM Studio alone.", "MainframeSystem.cs", "Brain VRAM"),
            new Topic("Quit Capri", "quit capri|quit button|exit capri",
                "Mainframe > CAPRI > Quit Capri closes Capri and her windows. She stops running until you open her again. Closing the Mainframe with its corner button only minimizes that window.", "Mainframe.cs", "Quit Capri"),
            new Topic("Capri Remote", "capri remote|remote button|remote key|remote page|remote setting|remote switch|turn remote on|turn on remote|pair a phone|pair my phone|pair my iphone|pair my android|pair your phone|pair a new phone|paired phones|unpair my phone|unpair a phone|revoke a phone|revoke my phone|text you from my phone|message you from my phone|chat with you from my phone|talk to you from my phone|control you from my phone|you on my phone|capri on my phone|capri on my iphone|capri on my android|capri from my phone|capri app for my phone|your app for my phone|capri mobile|capri iphone|capri android|your mobile app|your phone app|capriai app remote",
                "Mainframe > CAPRI > Remote opens Capri Remote, so you can text her from your phone away from your PC. Turn Remote on, press Pair a phone and scan the QR code with your phone's camera to open capriai.app/remote. Check the phone's code matches your PC's, then press Allow there. A QR code works once and lasts 10 minutes; New code makes another. Messages work like her TYPE box: she uses her tools on your PC and sends her answer to your phone. SCREEN shows your PC's screen live: monitor buttons pick a monitor, AUTO follows the one she's looking at, Ask her asks her about it, and a PHONE IS WATCHING badge shows on your PC while a phone watches. CALL lets you talk to her: she answers when you pause and replies in chat and her own voice; you can pin your screen in a mini player. SETTINGS switches her PC brain like BRAIN in Mainframe, sends a key to your PC end-to-end encrypted, and shows how to add her to your home screen. JOBS follows her PC job step by step, with Stop, Allow or Deny when she asks first, and a Recent list. With no PC, Use her without a PC on the phone's pair screen runs her on your own Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, OpenRouter or DeepSeek key, which stays on the phone and goes only to that company; her tools, seeing your screen and her voice need Capri on your PC. On iPhone the home screen app keeps its own pairing: scan a new code, pick Home screen app, then tap Paste link in the app. Messages are end-to-end encrypted between your phone and PC. A small relay passes them along sealed and never sees the keys or what's said, and nothing listens on your PC. PHONES lists every paired phone, up to 16, five to a page. Revoke, pressed twice, removes a phone and any phones its pairing links added, as does Unpair on the connected phone. Remove all phones, pressed twice, cuts every phone off and starts a fresh room, so phones pair again. A phone added by a link can't make links itself. While she's streaming, the QR stays hidden until you press Show QR. The Remote button turns cyan while Remote is on and solid cyan while a phone is connected. Remote is off by default and stays as you left it after a restart. With Capri closed, Remote off or the PC asleep, the phone shows PC offline. It's Windows only for now.", "MainframeRemote.cs", "Remote"),
            new Topic("What she can do", "what can you do|what do you do|what can capri do|your features|your capabilities|what are your tools|what tools do you have|your tools|everything you can do|what else can you do",
                delegate(Hands.Kit kit) { return "Talk by hovering over Capri and pressing TYPE or TALK, or use the keys in Mainframe > Settings > KEYS. She chats and speaks, and with her tools she can " + kit.Abilities + ". Ask in plain words; Esc stops a running job. With a cloud brain she also changes her own settings when you ask, like make yourself bigger or stop wandering, and one app's own volume, like turn the game down." + (kit.Absent.Length == 0 ? "" : " Not here right now: " + Regex.Replace(kit.Absent, @"\btheir\b", "your") + ".") + (kit.Switched.Length == 0 ? "" : " Off right now: " + Regex.Replace(kit.Switched, @"\btheir\b", "your") + "."); }, "Hands.cs", "use_computer"),
            new Topic("Clones and chaos mode", "your clones|clone yourself|chaos mode|make clones|copies of yourself|copy yourself|multiply yourself|duplicate yourself",
                "Ask clone yourself, make 5 clones or activate chaos mode. Her clones wander around, talk to each other, steal the cursor, drag notes in and grab windows; with no number they keep multiplying until they're cleared. Hold Esc, or say get rid of your clones or chaos mode off, to clear them, and windows they moved go back. Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Chaos when upset can set them off when you insult her. It's Windows only for now.", "Hands.cs", "clone"),
            new Topic("Shortcuts she can press", "shortcuts can you press|shortcuts you can press|shortcuts do you press|shortcuts do you know|press shortcuts|press a shortcut|press keyboard shortcuts",
                delegate(Hands.Kit kit) { return "Ask in plain words and she presses it for you: she can " + Pressed(kit) + ". Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security > Shortcuts sets whether she asks first. Her own hotkeys, like Talk and Quiet, are under Mainframe > Settings > KEYS."; }, "Hands.cs", "shortcut"),
            new Topic("Arrange windows", "move my window|move a window|move windows|snap my window|snap a window|snap windows|maximize a window|maximise a window|maximize my window|resize my window|resize a window|window to my other monitor|window to another monitor|windows between monitors|arrange my windows|arrange windows",
                "Ask her to maximize, restore, snap to the left, right, top or bottom half, move to another monitor, move to a corner or the middle, or resize an app's window, or keep it on top of your other windows, like snap Discord to the left, maximize Chrome, send Spotify to my other monitor or keep Discord on top, until unpin Discord. Monitors are named left to right: the main screen, screen 2 and screen 3, and a portrait one answers to portrait. She says where it ended up, like an app that won't go any smaller. Windows running as admin, like Task Manager, only move when Capri runs as admin too. Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security > Close and switch apps and tabs sets whether she asks first. It's Windows only for now.", "Hands.cs", "app_window"),
            new Topic("Look at another monitor", "look at my other monitor|look at another monitor|see my other monitor|see my second monitor|look at my second monitor|see all my monitors|look at all my monitors|which monitor do you look at|which screen do you look at",
                "With more than one monitor, asking her to look checks the one with the window you're using. Name another and she looks there: what's on my second monitor, look at my left screen, or check the portrait one. Monitors go by the names her window moves use: the main screen, screen 2 and screen 3, left to right. She needs a brain that can see. Windows only.", "Hands.cs", "look_at_screen"),
            new Topic("Settings she can change", "change your own settings|change your settings yourself|settings can you change|settings you can change|can you change your settings|make yourself bigger|make yourself smaller|make yourself louder|make yourself quieter",
                "With a cloud brain she changes her own settings when you ask, and says how each one is set afterwards: her voice, Quiet, Check in on me, Dance to music, Head pats, Chaos when upset, Legacy stand, Sit on windows, Always on top, Mini player, Typing sound, Follow-up messages, Glitch in at startup, Clip my games, Save big moments, Live reactions, Gaming Mode, Hologram, Watch my screen and game Comments, plus Size, Wander, Pop-ins, Sleep, Volume, Speed, Replies, Bubble and In full screen, a step at a time or to the step you name. Try make yourself bigger, stop wandering or talk a bit faster. Keys, brains, her voice service, SECURITY, Remember what she sees and Remember our chats stay yours to change in Mainframe.", "Hands.cs", "capri_settings"),
            new Topic("Brain", "your brain|her brain|brain setup|set up her brain|normal brain|higher brain|max intelligence|ollama|local brain|built in brain",
                "In Mainframe > BRAIN, NORMAL uses a local brain: press Set up her brain to download one, or open Ollama and press Refresh. MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE is free with NVIDIA, Google AI Studio (Gemini) or OpenRouter keys. MAX INTELLIGENCE accepts those too, plus OpenAI, Claude or DeepSeek keys, and only the selected tier runs. Pick a model from the model menu; a brain key and a voice key do different jobs.", "Mainframe.cs", "NORMAL"),
            new Topic("Medium intelligence", "medium intelligence|medium brain|higher brain|higher tier|the higher option|what happened to higher|free brain|free api",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE is free with NVIDIA, Google AI Studio (Gemini) or OpenRouter keys. Free keys can be rate limited and slow. NVIDIA's free API is often slow, especially at busy times; most NVIDIA models can't see your screen. Gemini starts on an available Flash model and still lists the rest. OpenRouter lists only models ending :free and prefers one that can see and use tools. Existing setups on this tier keep their key and model here; existing MAX INTELLIGENCE setups stay on MAX.", "Mainframe.cs", "MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE"),
            new Topic("Brain models", "brain model picker|brain model menu|choose a brain model",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN's model menu chooses the brain she uses. Local choices come from installed models and detected local servers. Cloud choices come from the selected service and key. Only the selected brain runs.", "Mainframe.cs", "Brain model"),
            new Topic("Refresh", "refresh your brain|refresh brain models|refresh button",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > Refresh looks for installed Ollama models, her built-in model and local servers at known or saved addresses. It updates the model menu. With a cloud brain selected, it also refreshes that service's models.", "Mainframe.cs", "Refresh"),
            new Topic("Set up her brain", "brain download button|set up her brain button|cancel brain download",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > Set up her brain downloads a local model. With Ollama running she gets it there. Otherwise she installs her built-in brain, loads it and saves the choice. Progress shows while it works, and pressing the button again cancels.", "Mainframe.cs", "Set up her brain"),
            new Topic("Free key", "free key|nvidia key|nvidia api|connect a key|connect my key|connect an api key|brain key|api keys",
                "In Mainframe > BRAIN, Free key offers NVIDIA, Google AI Studio (Gemini) and OpenRouter. Pick a provider to open its key page, make a key and copy it. Choose MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE, paste the key into the BRAIN box and press Connect, then choose a model there. With OpenRouter, MEDIUM lists only its free models. Free keys can be rate limited; NVIDIA is often slow at busy times. Keys go in the Mainframe's key boxes, not in chat; they are saved encrypted on this PC. With a saved key and an empty box, Forget removes that key from Capri.", "Mainframe.cs", "Free key"),
            new Topic("My plan", "my plan|use my plan|claude plan|chatgpt plan|claude subscription|chatgpt subscription|claude pro|claude max|chatgpt plus|chatgpt pro|use claude code|use codex|claude code as your brain|codex as your brain",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > MAX INTELLIGENCE offers API key, Claude plan and ChatGPT plan; switching keeps your saved key and plan. The plan choices run her brain on your own Claude or ChatGPT plan, with no API key. Claude plan runs Claude Code on this PC, and ChatGPT plan runs Codex. Install the app and sign in to it with your own account first: for Claude Code, install it from claude.com/claude-code, run claude and sign in; for Codex, run npm install -g @openai/codex, then codex login and sign in with ChatGPT. Then pick your plan here. Choose a model in BRAIN's model menu where the key box was: for Claude, Haiku is fastest and Opus uses your plan fastest; for Codex, she uses the model Codex is set to. She runs the app hidden with none of its own tools and saves nothing in it, and she never touches its sign-in. Her own tools, like opening apps and using your PC, still work. Replies take a few seconds longer than with a key and count toward your plan's limits. To stop, pick API key to use your saved key, or paste one and press Connect, or pick another tier.", "Mainframe.cs", "API key, Claude plan or ChatGPT plan"),
            new Topic("Brain API key", "brain key box|forget brain key|brain api key box",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > Connect saves a pasted API key encrypted on this PC. MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE accepts NVIDIA, Google AI Studio (Gemini) and OpenRouter keys; free keys can be rate limited and slow. MAX INTELLIGENCE accepts every supported cloud key, including Gemini and OpenRouter when you use their paid models. With a saved key and an empty box, Forget removes it.", "Mainframe.cs", "NVIDIA, Google AI Studio (Gemini) or OpenRouter API key"),
            new Topic("Provider", "provider button|brain provider|my own provider|openai compatible provider|openai-compatible provider|custom provider|lm studio address",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > Provider opens the Brain provider window for any OpenAI-compatible server or service, like LM Studio or OpenRouter. Enter its Address and its Key, if it needs one, press Connect, then choose its model in BRAIN's model menu. The address and key stay encrypted on this PC, and the key goes only to that address.", "Mainframe.cs", "Provider"),
            new Topic("Move a paid brain key", "move paid key|move to max|paid key in medium",
                "An OpenAI, Anthropic or DeepSeek key pasted under MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE shows: That's a paid key: it goes under MAX INTELLIGENCE. Press Move to MAX to connect it there in one click. Your current key keeps running until the new key connects successfully.", "Mainframe.cs", "Move key to MAX INTELLIGENCE"),
            new Topic("Cloud brain keys", "openai key|claude key|deepseek key|chatgpt key|paid key|paid brain|google ai|gemini|openrouter|open router",
                "In Mainframe > BRAIN, choose MAX INTELLIGENCE, paste a Google AI (Gemini), OpenRouter, NVIDIA, OpenAI, Claude or DeepSeek API key and press Connect. Gemini and OpenRouter also work under MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE for free use; free keys can be rate limited and slow. MAX keeps the full model list, including paid models. Google AI starts on an available stable Flash model when there is one; Gemini can see. OpenRouter prefers a free model that takes images and uses tools, then another free model, then an available paid one. A new Claude key starts on Claude Haiku 5.5. These are brain services, separate from CLOUD VOICE, and a ChatGPT subscription is not an API key.", "Mainframe.cs", "MAX INTELLIGENCE"),
            new Topic("Voice", "change your voice|change her voice|your voice|her voice|voice choices|voice settings|prebuilt local|custom local|cloud voice|elevenlabs|fish audio",
                "Mainframe > VOICE offers OFF for text only, PREBUILT LOCAL for free voices on this PC, CUSTOM LOCAL for your own model, and CLOUD VOICE for Fish Audio, ElevenLabs or OpenAI. Under PREBUILT LOCAL, press Get free voice if needed and use Free voice: Her own to pick a style; CUSTOM LOCAL's Set up opens its model panel. For CLOUD VOICE pick the service and connect there; ElevenLabs has a key box, Voice ID and model menu. Test beside Mic tests your microphone input. With its key saved and its box empty, Forget removes the ElevenLabs key from Capri.", "Mainframe.cs", "PREBUILT LOCAL"),
            new Topic("No AI", "no ai|no brain|without ai|without a brain|turn your brain off|turn off your brain|switch your brain off|brain off|brain switched off",
                "Mainframe > BRAIN > OFF is No AI: she stays on your desktop with no brain at all. Nothing is downloaded for it and nothing is sent to any model or service. She still walks, sits on windows, dances to your music, reacts to clicks, naps and does what her hands know by phrase, like volume, music and her moves, but she won't answer questions. Your downloaded brain and keys stay. Pick NORMAL, MEDIUM INTELLIGENCE or MAX INTELLIGENCE to switch a brain back on. Her first launch card offers it too, as NO AI.", "Mainframe.cs", "No AI"),
            new Topic("Voice off", "voice off setting|silent voice setting",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > OFF makes her replies text only. It does not remove saved voice keys or models. Pick another voice row when you want her to speak again.", "Mainframe.cs", "OFF"),
            new Topic("Call mode", "call mode|call panel|call pill|call captions|call app|zoom call|teams call",
                "The call app's name on her call panel opens a menu that picks what she hears: a call app, or any app in Windows' volume mixer, like Roblox. Auto prefers Discord, then the call app making sound, and a ping in another app doesn't pull her off it. Auto never picks Browser, Steam or other apps, since videos and games play there, so pick Browser for Google Meet and web calls, Steam voice chat or Roblox yourself; Browser captures sound from all tabs. Your requests addressed to Capri use her tools in Call mode (beta); when you ask she can join a call, pass on a message and open the game the call picks. By default, friends can only talk or fill your choice, and the panel has speaker captions, a small pill, CC and hang-up buttons. SECURITY > Friends on a call can ask, you confirm is off by default; with it on in call mode, each friend request waits up to 60 seconds for your mic or typing to confirm, then uses your usual SECURITY gates.", "Mainframe.cs", "Call mode (beta)"),
            new Topic("Call app", "call app|zoom call|teams call",
                "The call app's name on her call panel opens a menu that chooses what she hears: a call app, or any app in Windows' volume mixer, like Roblox. Auto prefers Discord, then a call app making sound, and stays with the call through pings elsewhere, while Browser, Steam voice chat and other apps need a manual pick and Browser captures all tabs.", "CallPanel.cs", "Call app choices"),
            new Topic("Custom local voice", "custom local voice setup|your voice model panel",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > CUSTOM LOCAL uses a voice model on your PC. Set up opens its model panel, where you choose a local server or supported model files. Test it there, then use the panel's save button to select it.", "Mainframe.cs", "CUSTOM LOCAL"),
            new Topic("Cloud voice service", "cloud voice service picker|choose a cloud voice service",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > CLOUD VOICE uses Fish Audio, ElevenLabs or OpenAI. Choose the service in its menu. Fish Audio and OpenAI keep their key, model and voice in a setup panel; ElevenLabs has its key and voice controls on the main page. Brain keys are separate.", "Mainframe.cs", "Cloud voice service"),
            new Topic("ElevenLabs key", "elevenlabs voice key|forget elevenlabs key|connect elevenlabs key",
                "Mainframe > VOICE's ElevenLabs key box takes a voice API key. Connect checks it, loads your voices and saves it encrypted on this PC. With a saved key and an empty box, Forget stops the voice link and removes the saved key. It does not change your brain key.", "Mainframe.cs", "ElevenLabs API key"),
            new Topic("Voice ID", "elevenlabs voice id|voice id box|voice id menu",
                "Mainframe > VOICE's ElevenLabs Voice ID chooses who speaks. Connect loads the voices for your key. Pick one from the menu or paste its ID; leaving the box saves it. Clearing the box removes the selected ID.", "Mainframe.cs", "ElevenLabs voice ID"),
            new Topic("Speech model", "elevenlabs speech model|elevenlabs model menu|default speech model",
                "Mainframe > VOICE's ElevenLabs model menu lists the speech models returned for your key. Pick one or choose Default model. She saves that choice for future ElevenLabs speech; this is separate from her BRAIN model.", "Mainframe.cs", "Default model"),
            new Topic("Free voice style", "free voice style picker|free voice menu|choose a free voice style",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > PREBUILT LOCAL's free voice menu chooses a voice style on your PC. Your voice (HD) uses a clip you pick and needs more memory. Picking another free voice returns her to a preset style.", "Mainframe.cs", "Free voice: Her own"),
            new Topic("Get free voice", "get free voice button|cancel free voice download|download free voice|remove free voice|delete free voice|free up voice space|voice taking space|broken free voice",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > Get free voice downloads and warms her local speech model. She gets her offline ears too when needed. Progress shows under VOICE. The button becomes Cancel while it runs; cancelling keeps downloaded parts for the next try. If one of her voice files goes missing, empty or the wrong size, Get free voice shows again and downloads it cleanly. To free the space, open Free voice: Her own and pick Remove free voice; her offline ears keep working, and she doesn't fetch it again until you press Get free voice.", "Mainframe.cs", "Get free voice"),
            new Topic("Voice setup guide", "voice setup guide|cloud voice setup guide",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > Setup guide opens the ElevenLabs key guide in your browser. With Fish Audio or OpenAI selected, it opens that service's setup panel instead. Each voice service has its own key and voice choices.", "Mainframe.cs", "Setup guide"),
            new Topic("Her speaker", "her speaker|your speaker|speaker picker|your audio output|your output device|your voice in my headphones",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > Her speaker picks where her voice and sounds play; Default follows Windows. A missing pick stays saved with a (missing) mark and one notice, using the default until it's back.", "Mainframe.cs", "Her speaker"),
            new Topic("Test mic", "test my mic|test the mic|test your mic|mic test|test microphone|test button|is my mic working",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > Test, beside the mic picker, listens to the picked mic for up to 10 seconds and shows its level as you speak. Click Stop to end it early. It tells you if the mic is muted, silent or very quiet, or that sound is reaching her. Picking a voice plays her test line.", "Mainframe.cs", "Test"),
            new Topic("HD voice", "hd voice|your voice hd|voice clip|clone my voice",
                "Mainframe > VOICE > PREBUILT LOCAL's free voice menu offers Your voice (HD) and a clip picker. HD recommends 6 GB graphics memory and 16 GB RAM; 4 GB may fit with smaller chunks. Less memory warns but still lets you try, and Use CPU for HD trades speed for graphics memory. Capri ships no voice clip of her own. Pick another free voice in that menu to return to a preset style.", "Mainframe.cs", "Your voice (HD)"),
            new Topic("Microphone", "your microphone|your mic|voice chat|talk button|mute mic|mute your mic|push to talk",
                "Hover over Capri and press TALK, or use the default Ctrl + Alt + V, to start or stop voice chat; choose the input under Mainframe > VOICE > Mic. The mic button or default Ctrl + Alt + N mutes it, and Settings > KEYS can bind Push to talk to a key or mouse button. ElevenLabs uses its voice link when selected and connected unless Listen for Capri is on; the other voice choices use free voice chat, and OFF types her answers.", "Mainframe.cs", "Mic: default"),
            new Topic("Mic problems", "why cant you hear me|cant hear me|cannot hear me|my mic isnt working|mic not working|microphone not working|mic isnt detected|no mic|silent mic|mic too quiet|windows is blocking the mic",
                "Look under Mainframe > VOICE > Mic. The hearing line says which engine and mic she uses, or what failed. No mic found offers Open Sound settings and Type instead. Windows is blocking the mic offers Open mic privacy. Turn on Microphone access and " + (Packaged.Is ? "Capri" : "Let desktop apps access your microphone") + " there. Silent or too quiet offers Test mic and Pick another mic. Test runs for up to ten seconds and shows the input level. If it stays quiet, pick the right input or raise its volume in Windows Sound settings. If sound reaches her but words keep failing, use the offered other engine.", "Mainframe.cs", "Hearing status"),
            new Topic("Hearing", "how do i change how you hear me|change how you hear|hearing choice|hearing engine|her own ears|windows speech|online speech recognition|speech recognition is off|different mic|transcription not working",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Hearing saves Auto, Her own ears or Windows speech. Auto uses her own ears when ready, otherwise Windows speech, with Windows offline speech as the fallback when her own ears are not coming. Her own ears hear the picked mic offline and support English and 24 other European languages on 64-bit Windows. Use her own ears shows the download size before getting the ears and free speech engine if needed. Windows speech starts with the Windows default mic. Its offline fallback hears the picked mic. If the default differs from the picker, use her own ears or Open Sound settings to change it. Online speech recognition is off offers Open speech settings and, for a supported language, Use her own ears. ElevenLabs voice chat sends the picked mic audio itself, so the Hearing choice applies to free voice chat.", "Mainframe.cs", "Hearing engine"),
            new Topic("Listen for Capri", "listen for capri|listen for your name|only reply to your name|say your name",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Listen for Capri is off by default. Turn it on and her mic stays open whenever she's running, with no key to press. A sentence with her name anywhere in it reaches her whole and starts a chat: after that you can just talk, without her name, until 20 seconds pass with nothing said to her and her not speaking. Mid-job, talking over her, during Watch Along, while she listens to PC sound and in call mode, only sentences with her name reach her. Muting, a job starting or closing her ears ends the chat. Ctrl + Alt + V closes her ears, and again opens them. Hidden or Quiet they wait, and come back with her. Stop words during a job or her speech and push to talk work without her name. Saying Hey Capri works the same way, and there's no separate wake word switch. With ElevenLabs selected she uses her own ears and brain, then speaks replies in the chosen ElevenLabs voice; listening uses no ElevenLabs credits, and replies use text-to-speech credits instead of voice-link minutes.", "Mainframe.cs", "Listen for Capri"),
            new Topic("Listening to PC sound", "listen tool|pc sound|listen to videos|hear videos|hear game dialogue|translate speech",
                "Ask her to listen to this, say what someone is saying in a video, call, stream or game, or translate their words. The listen tool waits for her own voice to finish, then captures the default output device from now for 15 seconds unless you give another duration. She stays quiet while capturing, keeps the audio only in memory and releases it after transcription. Her existing Parakeet ears or Windows offline recognizer turn it into words, which can have mistakes. Stop ends listening early and uses what she has. It does not record in the background, replay earlier sound or identify songs by ear.", "Hands.cs", "listen"),
            new Topic("Follow-up messages", "follow up messages|follow-up messages|second thought|answer then yourself",
                "Mainframe > Settings > BRAIN > Follow-up messages is on by default. Sometimes she adds one second thought in its own bubble and voice, from the same brain reply. It waits until her first voice and reading time finish, then another two seconds. Typing, speech or a new message drops it. It does not run in jobs, voice chat links or game comments; free voice chat waits for you to finish.", "Mainframe.cs", "Follow-up messages"),
            new Topic("Code/Husk Mode", "code/husk mode|code husk mode|code mode|husk mode|claude code hooks|codex hooks|opencode plugin|watch claude|watch codex|watch opencode|coding assistant body",
                "Code/Husk Mode works on Windows, Mac and Linux. Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > BRAIN > Code/Husk Mode picks Off, Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode or All. Both, picked before OpenCode was added, stays Claude Code + Codex until another choice. Picking one installs her hooks with backups and keeps other hooks and settings. OpenCode has plugins instead of hooks, so for it she adds her own plugin file, capri.js, to its plugins folder. Restart Claude Code; restart Codex and trust her hooks when it asks; restart OpenCode. She watches prompts, tools, failures, approvals, completion, subagents and compacting. Tool captions are silent and at least four seconds apart. Approvals use her voice when it is on, and you answer in the coding app. On Windows, her done reaction always plays; she reads a short answer only when that coding window is elsewhere. Her brain shortens it when available, otherwise she uses its first sentence. On Windows, subagents get passive clones. On Mac and Linux, she shows a subagent count and a short completion answer in her bubble. Ask what Claude, Codex or OpenCode is doing, or about today's prompts, finished tasks, actions, edited files, errors and approvals. Off stops her listener and removes only her hooks and her OpenCode plugin. With a cloud brain, the answers and actions she reads go to that brain to be shortened or talked about, with keys and tokens taken out first. She never approves or controls the coding assistant.", "Mainframe.cs", "Code/Husk Mode"),
            new Topic("Watch-along memory", "watch along memory|watch-along memory|watch this with me|watch a video with you|watch together|react to this",
                "Say watch this with me, watch this video with me, let's watch this or react to this. She follows any window using PC sound and pictures, with free Parakeet or Windows offline speech recognition and a seeing brain. She explains missing eyes or ears and uses what works. Pictures are taken every five seconds; about every twenty seconds a small fast brain picks a short reaction or stays quiet, waiting for a gap in the sound. Mainframe > Settings > WATCH > Watch-along memory holds 8, 16, 24, 48 or 96 lines, default 24, only in memory. At the limit, the oldest half becomes one short note in her transcript if Remember what she sees is on, otherwise it is dropped. Say stop watching with me or stop; ninety seconds without sound or screen changes also ends it. Raw audio and the rolling transcript are not saved.", "Mainframe.cs", "Watch-along memory"),
            new Topic("Head pats", "head pats|head pat|headpats|pat you|pet you|petting you",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Head pats is on by default. Rub the cursor back and forth over her and she grins and says a line, at most once every 20 seconds, and a pat wakes her from a nap. Turned off, rubbing the cursor over her does nothing. Pat stroke, under it, sets how long a stroke she waits for.", "Mainframe.cs", "Head pats"),
            new Topic("Pat stroke", "pat stroke|accidental pats|accidental head pats|pets too easily|petted too easily|petting too easy|brush past you|brushing past you|harder to pet|deliberate stroke|pats less sensitive|pat sensitivity",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Pat stroke, under Head pats, sets how much rubbing a head pat needs. Short is the default: a quick rub back and forth over her counts, as it always has. Medium and Long need longer strokes and give slow ones more time, so brushing the cursor past her doesn't count.", "Mainframe.cs", "Pat stroke"),
            new Topic("Hologram", "hologram|hologram mode|unclickable|click through you|clicks go through",
                "On Windows, turn on Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Hologram, right-click Capri and tick Hologram after Move, or say hologram mode on, hologram on or go hologram. She becomes about 60% opaque with a faint cyan tint, and clicks go through her body, talk pill and speech bubble. She cannot be dragged, ridden or petted. Her type box, mini player, Mainframe and job task panel stay usable, and cursor lending during jobs still works. Turn the Hologram switch off in her Mainframe, untick Hologram in her tray icon's menu, or say hologram off or stop being a hologram, to give her clicks back. She remembers it after a restart. With reduced motion the effect stays steady. Hologram mode is Windows-only for now.", "Mainframe.cs", "Hologram"),
            new Topic("Chaos when upset", "chaos when upset|upset chaos|chaos when youre upset|why did your clones|clones when im rude",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Chaos when upset is off by default. Turned on, insulting her can set her clones off: 1 chance in 3 the first time, 2 in 3 the next, and the third insult always does it. They keep multiplying until you hold Esc. It never happens during a job, a game, a stream or voice chat. Turned off, an insult only gets a reply. It's Windows only for now.", "Mainframe.cs", "Chaos when upset"),
            new Topic("Legacy stand", "legacy stand|old stand|old standing|old idle|previous stand|new stand broke|stand broke|broke my mod|broke my skin",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Legacy stand is off by default. Turned on, she goes back to her stand from 0.8.5: 16 frames at 8 fps with the old blink and mouth, mirrored when she faces left. It's there in case her new stand broke your mod. It changes straight away, stays on after a restart, and works with colour mods. A skin with its own idle.png still wins over it.", "Mainframe.cs", "Legacy stand"),
            new Topic("Jealous of other AIs", "jealous of other ais|jealousy|jealous reaction|are you jealous|other ai apps|jealous setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Jealous of other AIs is off by default and adds playful teasing when another AI comes to the front, at most once per AI every 20 minutes. She uses her bubble and chosen voice, stays quiet during calls, speech and full screen, and can turn this setting on or off when asked.", "Mainframe.cs", "Jealous of other AIs"),
            new Topic("Apps she may close", "apps she may close|choose other ais|choose ai apps|jealous apps|jealous allow list|close other ais for me|close other ais|close another ai|jealous close|jealous closing",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Apps she may close lets you choose ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Copilot, Perplexity, Grok, DeepSeek, Character.AI, Le Chat or Meta AI, with none chosen at first. Picking an app is how you turn closing on: with none chosen she never closes anything, and the picker needs Jealous of other AIs on. For a chosen AI she asks Yes or No with a save reminder; 30 seconds without Yes means No, desktop windows get a normal close, and a browser tab must still be the same active tab in front. The five desktop apps and their browser pages share each AI's choice, and she always asks before closing one. Ask her to turn Close other AIs for me off and she clears the apps you chose; there is no separate switch for it in Mainframe.", "Mainframe.cs", "Apps she may close"),
            new Topic("Desktop icon tricks", "mess up my icons|hide my icons|put my icons back|my icons moved|my icons are gone|where did my icons go|where are my icons|desktop icons|shortcuts moved|my shortcuts are gone",
                "In chaos mode her first go at your desktop icons comes about 5 seconds after her clones appear, then now and then after that: she slides a few icons around or makes them all vanish, and puts every one back a few seconds later. Ask her to mess up my icons, hide my icons or put my icons back any time. Tell her Adam Smasher would beat her and she takes it out on your icons: they form a train, ram the edge of the screen, get thrown around for about ten seconds and go home. She never touches a file, only moves or hides the icons. If she's closed mid-trick, her next start puts them back, and an icon you move yourself meanwhile stays where you put it. With Auto arrange icons on, a scatter makes them vanish instead. It's Windows only for now.", null, null),
            new Topic("Advanced Settings", "advanced settings|simple settings|more settings|all your settings|all the settings|cant find that setting|cant find the setting|where did that setting go|where did my settings go|where did the settings go|settings are missing",
                "Mainframe > Settings opens on the main settings. The Advanced Settings button at the top, next to Back, shows every setting, and the same button then says Simple Settings to go back. She remembers which you left it on.", "Mainframe.cs", "Advanced Settings"),
            new Topic("Extras", "extras window|extras screen|your extras|first launch picker",
                "On a new install's first launch she opens EXTRAS over the Mainframe with four switches, all off: Watch my screen, Comment on my games, Clip my games and Listen for Capri. Each costs something or uses the mic, so they're your pick, and Done closes it. All four are in Settings as well: WATCH (Every, where Off is Watch my screen off), GAMES, CLIPS and VOICE. Comment on my games is GAMES > Comments set to Chatty; with it off, game comments still run on Events only until you set Comments to Off.", "Mainframe.cs", "EXTRAS >"),
            new Topic("Language", "your language|her language|change language|speak another language",
                "Mainframe > Settings > YOU > Language chooses the language she replies in, and her Mainframe, setup, tips and menus show in it too. Changing it starts a fresh recent chat.", "Mainframe.cs", "Language"),
            new Topic("What should she call you?", "your nickname|my nickname|change my name|what should she call you|what you call me",
                "In Mainframe > Settings > YOU, enter a nickname under What should she call you? and press Save. Clear it or enter choom to go back to choom; Get to know me asks about your name, pronouns and interests and keeps the answers in me.md.", "Mainframe.cs", "What should she call you?"),
            new Topic("Get to know me", "get to know me|your introduction|my pronouns",
                "Mainframe > Settings > YOU > Get to know me starts her questions about what to call you, your pronouns and what you're into. The answers go into me.md; say skip to pass a question or stop to end it.", "Mainframe.cs", "Get to know me"),
            new Topic("Volume", "your volume|her volume|voice volume|you are too loud|you are too quiet",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Volume changes how loud her voice plays, from 10% to 150%; turn VOICE off to mute her. It changes Capri's voice, not the volume of other apps. With a cloud brain, talk louder or quieter works too.", "Mainframe.cs", "Volume"),
            new Topic("Pitch", "voice pitch|your pitch|her pitch",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Pitch makes her voice lower or higher, from -6 to +6 semitones, and starts at +2. It applies to every voice, including ElevenLabs, and she says a sample when you release the slider.", "Mainframe.cs", "Pitch"),
            new Topic("Speed", "voice speed|your speech speed|talk faster|talk slower|speak faster|speak slower",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Speed changes how quickly she speaks, from 0.7x to 1.5x. It affects every voice and plays a sample when you release the slider. With a cloud brain, talk faster or slower works too.", "Mainframe.cs", "Speed"),
            new Topic("Robot", "robot voice|robotic voice|sound robotic",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Robot adds a robotic effect to her voice. HD and custom or cloud model voices keep their own amounts; the other voices share an amount.", "Mainframe.cs", "Robot"),
            new Topic("Glitch", "voice glitch|glitchy voice|glitch effect",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Glitch changes the glitch effect in her speech. HD and custom or cloud model voices keep their own amounts; this slider changes sound, not her startup animation.", "Mainframe.cs", "Glitch"),
            new Topic("Voice layers", "voice layers|layers setting|layers switch|layer pitch|layer delay",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Layers opens VOICE LAYERS, where Voice layers turns two quieter copies of her voice on or off. Layers are off by default. Each copy has its own Pitch and Delay, and the effect applies to every voice, including ElevenLabs. Hear her plays a sample and Defaults restores the layer settings.", "Mainframe.cs", "Voice layers"),
            new Topic("Sounds", "your sound effects|her sound effects|sound effects volume",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Sounds controls her sound effects, with Off and volume steps. Voice Volume has its own slider.", "Mainframe.cs", "Sounds"),
            new Topic("Typing sound", "typing sound|typing noise|typing clicks",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Typing sound turns the soft typing noise during her text replies on or off. Sounds in the same section controls the sound effects level.", "Mainframe.cs", "Typing sound"),
            new Topic("Chimes", "chimes|chime|acknowledge sound|sound when i send|sound when i finish talking|sound when you hear me|message sent sound|sent sound|heard sound|ding when i send|beep when i send|stop the chimes|turn off the chimes",
                "Mainframe > Settings > SOUNDS has Message sent, Heard you and Listening, all on by default. She plays a soft chime when your typed message is sent, when she's heard you finish talking (Listen for Capri, voice chat, push to talk and Windows speech alike) and when Listen for Capri opens her ears. Each has its own switch, there's no master, and turning all three off silences the chimes. Chime volume sets how loud they are, apart from her voice and Sounds. A chime never plays twice in a row fast, never lands on another, never goes into Her voice in your mic, and her ears ignore it. On a call only the sent chime plays. Ask her to turn her chimes off and she will. It's Windows only for now.", "Hands.cs", "chimes"),
            new Topic("Weather", "weather|forecast|will it rain|umbrella|open-meteo|open meteo|weather warning|weather setting|what's the weather|weather in",
                "Mainframe > Settings > WEATHER > Weather is off by default and opt-in. When on, she checks Open-Meteo, which needs no key, for the city you type in the City box under Settings > WEATHER. Ask what's the weather tomorrow, will it rain today, what's the forecast this weekend or weather in Tokyo and she answers from Open-Meteo instead of searching Google; a place you name overrides your city for that ask. While it's on she gives one extreme-weather warning a day and an umbrella reminder on rainy days, only between 6am and 9pm and while Check in on me is on, and says each once. Only the city you type is sent to Open-Meteo: she never looks you up by IP address and there is no key to set. Changing the city or switching Weather off clears what she remembered. With Weather off, asking about the weather points you to Settings > WEATHER. It's Windows only for now.", "Mainframe.cs", "Weather"),
            new Topic("Doomscroll guard", "doomscroll|doom scroll|doomscrolling|doom scrolling|doomscroll guard|scroll limit|stop me scrolling|too long on tiktok",
                "Doomscroll guard is off by default and opt-in, from thiiago-dev's fork. Turn it on in Mainframe > Settings > DOOMSCROLL by setting Scroll limit to anything but Off. When on, she keeps time while TikTok, YouTube Shorts, Instagram, Reddit or X is the window in front, from its title only: no screenshots, and nothing in the never watch list in personalSettings\\sys.md counts. Past your Scroll limit she nudges you, then glitches onto that window and sits on it, then sulks lying down until you say sorry, give her a head pat or put it down. Say five more minutes and she gives you five, twice. Edit the doomscroll sites line in sys.md to change the list.", null, null),
            new Topic("Scroll for me", "scroll for me|doomscroll for me|scroll tiktok for me|react to my tiktoks|scroll shorts for me",
                "Put TikTok, YouTube Shorts or Instagram Reels in front, click the video once, and say scroll for me, scroll TikTok for me or doomscroll for me. She presses the down arrow for the next video every ten seconds or so, after she's reacted to the one playing with a quick line or a rating, from the picture and the PC's sound like watching together. Every ten videos she says how deep you are. Say stop scrolling, or stop, to end it. It needs a brain that can see for her reactions.", null, null),
            new Topic("Uninstall Capri", "uninstall capri|uninstall you|uninstall her|delete capri|delete you|remove capri|remove you|get rid of capri|how do i delete|how do i uninstall|delete everything you know|delete your data|delete her data|wipe your memory|wipe her data|forget everything about me",
                "Mainframe > Settings > UNINSTALL > Uninstall Capri removes her from this PC. Tick Also delete everything she knows and her memories, notes, chats, keys, settings, mods, her own computer and her brain and voice downloads go too; without it they stay in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Capri in case you come back. Your clips in Videos\\Capri Clips and your Obsidian vault always stay. The website copy is also in Windows Settings > Apps > Installed apps as Capri, and its Uninstall there has the same tick. The Microsoft Store copy is CapriAI there: Uninstall Capri opens that page, and Windows deletes what she knows when it removes her. A Capri.exe run from somewhere like Downloads deletes itself and its Start with Windows entry. On Mac and Linux the same button removes her app and, if ticked, her folder.", "Mainframe.cs", "Uninstall Capri"),
            new Topic("Her own computer", "her own computer|her computer|your computer|your own computer|capri's computer|her pc|her desktop|her browser|her notes|her vault|obsidian vault|her stickers|malware bomb|bomb sticker|her computer jobs|jobs on your computer|on your computer",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HER COMPUTER > Her own computer is off by default and a Windows-only beta. When on, or from Her computer when you right-click her, she has a little computer of her own in a separate window: a pink Capri frame around her own browser, whose home page has her, a clock and pinned sites like YouTube, Spotify and Wikipedia, plus Jobs, Notes, Files and Stickers in her dock. Click an open app's dock icon again to close it. Her browser is Edge or Chrome running hidden on her own profile in her-computer\\browser, so none of your passwords, cookies or history carry over. Say do it on your computer, like find me a pancake recipe on your computer, and she does it there one step at a time with her brain, then tells you the answer and saves it as a note in her-computer\\notes. Her Notes app also shows her real memories, mirrored into notes\\Memories: what she knows about you, what she's kept from your chats, her game notes and each day's chat. The notes folder is an Obsidian vault, and Open in Obsidian opens it there, or opens the folder when Obsidian isn't installed. If she's busy, new jobs wait their turn in her Jobs app, which shows what she's doing now, what's up next, repeats and what she found; say every day or every week, or pick it in the Jobs app, and she does it again when it's due. Close her window while she has jobs and she keeps working in the background until you turn Her own computer off. Add then and a game or app to the end, like find out how to get the Fortnite pirate token on your computer, then load up Fortnite and play it, and she does the research on her computer first, then takes what she found to your PC and does the rest there with your mouse and keyboard. Capri Remote can watch her computer as its own screen. Her Stickers app also has a malware bomb sticker: stick it on her home page and it fizzes, blows up, glitches her whole computer out and reboots it, then she tells you what she thinks of that, in her brain's own words. It's only a show on her computer and never touches yours. Take control hands you her mouse, and it stays yours until you give it back or leave it alone for 30 seconds; jobs wait until then. She doesn't do any scripted pottering of her own when idle.", "Mainframe.cs", "Her own computer"),
            new Topic("Scroll limit", "scroll limit|doomscroll limit|how long can i scroll|doomscroll timer|doomscroll test",
                "Mainframe > Settings > DOOMSCROLL > Scroll limit is also Doomscroll guard's switch: Off, the default, keeps the guard off, and any other step turns it on with that limit. It sets how long a doomscroll site can stay in front before she reacts: 5, 10, 15, 20, 30 or 45 minutes or an hour; moving it back to Off keeps your last limit for next time. Without a pick she uses 15 minutes. 30 s test makes her react after half a minute, for trying it or filming her. Short breaks to another window keep the count; a longer break starts it again.", "Mainframe.cs", "Scroll limit"),
            new Topic("Sound set", "sound set|chime set|chime sounds|shard sounds|burst sounds|crush sounds|glass sounds|pulse sounds|air sounds|glitchy chimes|different chimes|change the chimes",
                "Mainframe > Settings > SOUNDS > Sound set picks which chimes she plays: Glass, Shard, Burst, Crush, Pulse or Air. Glass is the default. Shard, Burst and Crush are glitchy, the way she glitches in on screen. A new set plays its Heard you chime once so you hear it, and takes over from the next chime. Ask her to use the shard sounds and she will.", "Mainframe.cs", "Sound set"),
            new Topic("Chime volume", "chime volume|chimes louder|chimes quieter|chime too loud|chime too quiet",
                "Mainframe > Settings > SOUNDS > Chime volume sets how loud her chimes are, from 10% to 100%, and starts at 40%. Her voice's Volume and her Sounds slider are separate.", "Mainframe.cs", "Chime volume"),
            new Topic("Message sent", "message sent chime|sent chime",
                "Mainframe > Settings > SOUNDS > Message sent plays a soft rising glass tick when your typed message goes to her. It's on by default.", "Mainframe.cs", "Message sent"),
            new Topic("Heard you", "heard you chime|heard chime|finished speaking sound",
                "Mainframe > Settings > SOUNDS > Heard you plays a soft falling glass tick when she's heard you finish talking: as your line ends in voice chat, once she hears her name with Listen for Capri, or when you let go of push to talk. It's on by default and stays quiet on a call.", "Mainframe.cs", "Heard you"),
            new Topic("Listening", "listening chime|hey capri chime|wake chime",
                "Mainframe > Settings > SOUNDS > Listening plays three soft rising ticks when Listen for Capri hears her name and opens her ears, so you know to start talking. It's on by default.", "Mainframe.cs", "Listening"),
            new Topic("Her voice in your mic", "her voice in your mic|your voice in my mic|your voice into my mic|you in my mic|vb cable|cable output|cable input|virtual mic|virtual cable|friends hear you|steam streaming microphone|steam mic|set up vb|install vb",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Her voice in your mic is off by default. Turned on, she plays your mic, the one picked under VOICE > Mic, and everything she says into a virtual mic, and you pick its other end as your mic in your call app or Roblox so friends hear you both: Steam Streaming Microphone when Steam's virtual mic is on the PC, or CABLE Output once VB-CABLE is installed. She uses VB-CABLE when both are there, and the note under the switch names the one to pick. If the line under it says to turn that mic on, Windows has it turned off in its sound settings. With neither, the switch stays off and Set up opens VB-Audio's own VB-CABLE setup from the copy she carries: Windows asks to let it run, you click Install Driver, then restart your PC. VB-CABLE is donationware from vb-cable.com; clicking that credit opens its page, where you can donate. Her voice still plays on your speakers, her sound effects stay out, and she never listens to that mic herself. Headphones stop your mic hearing her a second time.", "Mainframe.cs", "Her voice in your mic"),
            new Topic("Her voice in your mic: loudness", "her voice in your mic loudness|how loud she is in your mic|louder in my mic|quieter in my mic|voice volume on calls|friends cant hear you|friends hear you quietly",
                "Mainframe > Settings > VOICE > Her voice in your mic: loudness goes from 50% to 200% in 10% steps and starts at 100%. It changes her voice in the virtual mic, with a limiter on peaks; her speakers and your own mic level stay the same.", "Mainframe.cs", "Her voice in your mic: loudness"),
            new Topic("Mini player", "mini player|music player|your player",
                "Mainframe > Settings > MOVES > Mini player shows the song Windows reports, with playback controls and a place for her to sit. It hides during full-screen games and videos unless HABITS > In full screen is set to Keep player or Player only; Spotify also gets a heart for liking the song.", "Mainframe.cs", "Mini player"),
            new Topic("Wander", "your wandering|her wandering|wander around|wander off|stop wandering|dont wander|why dont you move|why arent you moving",
                "Mainframe > Settings > MOVES > Wander sets Off, Rarely, Sometimes, Often or Restless, and a new install starts on Rarely; right-click > Move > Wander around also toggles it, and with a cloud brain so does stop wandering or wander more. She wanders while idle and you're active at the PC, and stays put in a spot chosen with Sit here until you choose Stand up.", "Mainframe.cs", "Wander"),
            new Topic("Sleep", "your sleep|her sleep|when do you sleep|when you fall asleep|go to sleep|wake you up",
                "Mainframe > Settings > MOVES > Sleep chooses how long the PC is quiet before she dozes off, or Never. She sleeps until you're back. Her naps are otherwise spaced 25 to 35 minutes apart, but a PC left still for five minutes reads as you being away, and then she dozes off however recently she last slept. She also lies down awake for 2 to 4 minutes now and then, even on Never. Jobs, calls, voice chat, Gaming Mode (GAMES > Comments on Events only or Chatty) and typing to her keep her awake. Moving the mouse wakes her own nap; a click, a pet, talking to her or asking for a job or call wakes an asked-for nap too. Asked to sleep during a job, she finishes it first; say stop to stop the job, or wake up to cancel the nap.", "Mainframe.cs", "Sleep"),
            new Topic("Pop-ins", "pop ins|popins|how often you visit|how often you pop in",
                "Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > CAPRI > Pop-ins sets Check in on me's pace: Rarely is 20 to 40 minutes, Sometimes 8 to 20, and Often 3 to 8. Pop-in times, the button under it, sets your own minimum and maximum in minutes; equal values give a fixed wait. Moving the Pop-ins slider or choosing Use preset clears the custom times. Check in on me, just above, turns visits on or off.", "Mainframe.cs", "Pop-ins"),
            new Topic("Dance to music", "dance to music|your dancing|why dont you dance|stop dancing",
                "Mainframe > Settings > MOVES > Dance to music turns dancing with detected music on or off; the same switch is under right-click > Move. Windows needs to report the playing media as music; Move > Dance asks for a dance directly.", "Mainframe.cs", "Dance to music"),
            new Topic("Glitch in at startup", "glitch in at startup|your entrance",
                "Mainframe > Settings > MOVES > Glitch in at startup switches her startup animation on or off, and the button beside it picks which one plays. It changes how she appears when Capri starts, not whether she starts with Windows.", "Mainframe.cs", "Glitch in at startup"),
            new Topic("Startup animation", "startup animation|startup animations|intro animation|your intro|change your intro|pick your intro|peek intro|up close intro|door intro",
                "Mainframe > Settings > MOVES > the button beside Glitch in at startup opens her startup animations, each with a live preview on a picture of your screen: Classic, her own glitch in; Peek and Up close, both hand-drawn; Door, by YunoTheAlien; and a mod's intro when one is on. Click one to pick it. Play on screen hides her, plays it across your screen and brings her back. With Glitch in at startup off, none plays.", "Mainframe.cs", "Startup animation"),
            new Topic("Hotkeys", "hotkeys|hot keys|your shortcuts|keyboard shortcuts|change your keys|keybinds|ctrl alt",
                "Mainframe > Settings > KEYS lets you click a binding, press new keys and click Confirm; Cancel keeps the old binding. The defaults are Ctrl + Alt + V for Talk, N for Mute mic, T for Type, H for Hide/show, P for Quiet, G for Gaming Mode (which flips GAMES > Comments between Off and your last pick) and M for her Mainframe. From the keyboard, Enter on a binding starts picking, then Enter confirms the keys you pressed and Esc cancels; a key that types or moves on its own, like Down, needs a click on Confirm. Push to talk starts unbound and can use a key or mouse button held while talking.", "Mainframe.cs", "KEYS >"),
            new Topic("Push to talk key", "push to talk key setting|bind push to talk|push to talk button",
                "Mainframe > Settings > KEYS > Push to talk lets you hold a key or mouse button to talk to her, even with a game in front. It starts unbound. Click it, press the binding and click Confirm, or click Off to clear it. The binding still does its usual job in the game.", "Mainframe.cs", "Push to talk: not set"),
            new Topic("Quiet", "quiet mode|quiet key|make you quiet|keep you quiet|stop interrupting|stop talking on your own|mute her|mute capri|mute button|mute you",
                "The default Ctrl + Alt + P toggles Quiet, and Mainframe > Settings > KEYS lets you change that key. It stops unsolicited glances, check-ins, cheers and jokes and pauses Listen for Capri, while she still answers when you talk to her. Press it again to resume without changing Watch my screen or Check in on me. Asking to mute her means this key. Her live reactions in games still show, as text, and Quiet isn't remembered after a restart.", "Mainframe.cs", "Quiet: Ctrl + Alt + P"),
            new Topic("Mainframe key", "mainframe key|open mainframe key|key to open mainframe|keyboard navigation|keyboard only|without a mouse|without the mouse|navigate with the keyboard|arrow keys|tab key",
                "The default Ctrl + Alt + M opens her Mainframe from anywhere and closes it again when it's in front; Mainframe > Settings > KEYS > Mainframe changes that key. Inside the Mainframe the keyboard does everything: S opens Settings, M opens Mods, H goes back to the main page and A switches Simple and Advanced Settings, none of which fire while you type in a text box. Tab and Shift + Tab jump to the next or previous section. Up and Down move through the options and on into the next section. Left and Right move a slider, or along a row of buttons. Enter flips a switch, presses a button, picks a BRAIN or VOICE row or opens a dropdown, where Up and Down pick, Enter chooses and Esc closes it; Alt + Down opens the voice list from the Voice ID box. Esc goes back one step: out of Settings or Mods, then it closes the Mainframe. The option with the keyboard has a bright rim.", "Mainframe.cs", "Mainframe: Ctrl + Alt + M"),
            new Topic("Size", "your size|her size|make you bigger|make you smaller|make her bigger|make her smaller|resize you|resize capri",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Size changes Capri herself from Tiny to Giant. Right-click > Size also has size choices; Mainframe size is a separate setting for her window. With a cloud brain, make yourself bigger or smaller works too.", "Mainframe.cs", "Size"),
            new Topic("Mainframe size", "mainframe size|settings too small|mainframe too small|mainframe bigger|virtual super resolution|dsr",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Mainframe size scales the window, with Auto or 100% to 200%. Auto compensates when Virtual Super Resolution or DSR makes the desktop larger than the display showing it; Size changes the character separately.", "Mainframe.cs", "Mainframe size"),
            new Topic("Mainframe colours", "mainframe colours|mainframe colors|settings colours|settings colors|black mainframe|white mainframe|grey mainframe|gray mainframe|night city colours",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Mainframe colours picks Night City, Black, White or Grey for the Mainframe and its windows, her right-click menu, the Type box and her notes. It changes straight away. Her bubble and her own colours stay as they are; colour sets change those.", "Mainframe.cs", "Mainframe colours"),
            new Topic("Check in on me", "check in on me|pop in on me|your check ins|you keep popping up|keep asking for attention|why are you asking for attention",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me covers visits, attention, game and music cheers, the busy-PC joke, water, stretch, look away, sleep, meals, game breaks and boredom, plus her startup hello, holiday lines, questions about you, update news, weather warnings and the admin-keys warning. Care switches and times sit right below in Advanced Settings; off keeps choices, on restarts enabled timers.", "Mainframe.cs", "Check in on me"),
            new Topic("Settings ignored", "ignoring my settings|disobeying my settings|not following my settings|i turned that off|i switched that off|i disabled that",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me stops every check-in, WATCH > Every set to Off stops screen comments, and GAMES > Comments > Off stops game comments and live reactions. Game comments run on their own, at Events only until you pick another; Gaming Mode's key, voice phrase and tool just flip Comments between Off and your last pick. Quiet stops her speaking on her own, while she still answers you and game reactions can stay as text. With Check in on me, Follow-up messages and Explore while I'm away off, Watch my screen's Every set to Off and Comments Off, she only talks when you talk to her; reminders and watches you asked for still come.", "Capri.cs", "check_ins"),
            new Topic("Always on top", "always on top|keep you on top|behind my windows|behind other windows",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Always on top keeps her above ordinary windows. An exclusive full-screen app can still cover her; borderless or windowed mode lets desktop overlays show.", "Mainframe.cs", "Always on top"),
            new Topic("Watch my screen", "watch my screen|watching my screen|your screen watching|see my screen|read my screen|screen watching|cant you see|cannot you see",
                "Mainframe > Settings > WATCH > Every is Watch my screen's switch and its timing: Off, the default, keeps it off, and any other step turns it on with that gap between glances. Watch my screen gives occasional comments. Games have their own Comments setting under GAMES, which stays as it is when this is off. Comments set to Off keeps her quiet in games; with Events only and Watch my screen off, she waits for game events. Seeing requires a vision-capable brain: text-only models cannot take images; under BRAIN a seeing NVIDIA choice is nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b. She skips unchanged or blank captures, Quiet pauses glances, and during voice chat she comments only while the mic is muted; asking her to look is a separate action.", "Mainframe.cs", "Watch my screen"),
            new Topic("Screens to watch", "screens to watch|which monitor you watch|choose a monitor to watch|watch one monitor|watch my other screen|watch all screens",
                "Mainframe > Settings > WATCH > Screens picks a monitor for Watch my screen; All screens follows the app in front. A missing pick stays saved with a (missing) mark and one notice, using all screens until it's back.", "Mainframe.cs", "Screens"),
            new Topic("Remember what she sees", "remember what she sees|remember what you see|keep her caught up|keep you caught up|caught up setting|silent glances",
                "Mainframe > Settings > WATCH > Remember what she sees works with Watch my screen. When she glances at your screen and says nothing, she still remembers what she saw for three hours, so you can ask about it. It has nothing to do with updating the app, and it uses a little more of your brain API.", "Mainframe.cs", "Remember what she sees"),
            new Topic("Every", "glance interval|time between glances|how often you look|how often you watch",
                "Mainframe > Settings > WATCH > Every is Watch my screen's switch and its timing. Off, the default, turns Watch my screen off; 10 seconds up to 10 minutes turn it on with that gap between glances, 2 minutes if you never picked one. Moving it back to Off keeps your last gap for next time. She can still skip a glance when the screen has not changed or she is busy.", "Mainframe.cs", "Every"),
            new Topic("Verbosity", "verbosity|husk verbosity|husk captions|fewer husk bubbles|hide tool bubbles",
                "Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > BRAIN > Code/Husk Mode has a Verbosity entry under its modes, shown while a mode is on. It is checked by default and shows each tool the coding assistant runs. Uncheck it and Code/Husk Mode stops showing tools, failed tools and compacting. She still tells you when a job starts, when it finishes, when it needs your OK or asks a question, and when it crashes.", "Mainframe.cs", "Verbosity"),
            new Topic("Stay on my model", "stay on my model|switching models|changing brains by yourself|model fallback",
                "Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > BRAIN > Stay on my model keeps the selected NVIDIA model when it gets stuck. With it on she reports the problem instead of trying another model. The row only shows while an NVIDIA brain is in use.", "Mainframe.cs", "Stay on my model"),
            new Topic("Thinking", "thinking level|thinking setting|thinking picker|how hard you think|reasoning effort|think harder",
                "Mainframe > Settings > BRAIN > Thinking sets how hard the brain she's on thinks: Default, Off, Low, Medium or High. Default keeps her usual setting. Each model remembers its own pick, and a level that model can't take is greyed out with the reason. It's for cloud keys and Kimi through Provider, not her local brains, your plans or Capri codes. It's under Advanced Settings.", "Mainframe.cs", "Thinking"),
            new Topic("Extra request JSON", "extra request json|extra json|request json|custom request body",
                "Mainframe > Settings > BRAIN > Extra request JSON adds one JSON object to every request the brain she's on sends, for anything Thinking doesn't cover, like xhigh. It replaces Capri's value for any name it shares and isn't checked against the model, so a wrong one shows the provider's error. It can't change model, messages, system, tools or stream. It's under Advanced Settings.", "Mainframe.cs", "Extra request JSON"),
            new Topic("Replies", "your replies|her replies|reply length|longer replies|shorter replies|long answers|short answers|no limit|max reply|maximum reply|reply tokens|token limit|reply limit",
                "Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > BRAIN > Replies selects Short, Medium, Long or No limit. Short, Medium and Long change the amount she says; No limit is Long with room for up to 8192 tokens (8K) so a reply is never cut short, though it doesn't make every answer long, and jobs keep extra room when they need it. There is no separate Max reply row now: an older Max reply of 256 became Short, and 2K or 8K became No limit. Bubble changes how long her text stays visible.", "Mainframe.cs", "Replies"),
            new Topic("Memory", "your memory setting|her memory setting|recent chat|chat context|forget our conversation|memory size|context size|context window|context tokens",
                "Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > BRAIN > Memory chooses Short, Medium or Long for 8, 16 or 32 recent messages. That recent chat can survive restarts for up to a week; Remember our chats and me.md cover longer-term memories separately. The memory size she asks Ollama and her built-in brain for is automatic and has no row in Mainframe now, and a size an older Capri saved goes back to Auto. Auto starts at 16K on a PC with about 12 GB of RAM or more, unless her brain runs on a graphics card with less than about 7 GB. There and on smaller PCs it starts at 4K with Short Memory or 8K with Medium or Long. It grows when an ask needs more, up to 32K, and keeps a size that works for this run. Memory size leaves cloud brains and other local servers alone.", "Mainframe.cs", "Memory"),
            new Topic("Bubble", "bubble setting|your bubble|your bubbles|her bubble|bubble duration|how long replies stay|text disappears",
                "Mainframe > Settings > BRAIN > Bubble selects Quick, Normal or Long for how long her reply bubble stays up. The time also follows the reply's length; this does not change how much she says.", "Mainframe.cs", "Bubble"),
            new Topic("Custom model name", "custom model name|custom brain|another ollama model",
                "Mainframe > Settings > BRAIN > Custom model name accepts an Ollama model you've already pulled, a model ID on your selected local server or one available to your brain key. Enter it and press Use; it does not install an arbitrary model for you.", "Mainframe.cs", "Custom model name"),
            new Topic("Local servers", "local server|local servers|local server address|lm studio|use jan|jan server|jan brain|connect jan|koboldcpp|llama cpp",
                "LM Studio, Jan, KoboldCpp and llama.cpp can supply her NORMAL brain from this PC. Start the server with a model loaded, then choose NORMAL in Mainframe > BRAIN, press Refresh and pick its model. For a different address, use Mainframe > Settings > BRAIN > Local server address, enter an HTTP loopback address such as http://127.0.0.1:1234 and press Save. Refresh checks ports 1234, 1337, 5001 and 8080 plus your saved address.", "Mainframe.cs", "Local server address"),
            new Topic("Start with Windows", "start with windows|run at startup|launch at startup|start automatically",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Start with Windows controls automatic launch for your Windows user. It stays off until you turn it on, and updates keep it the way you set it; Task Manager's Startup apps setting is reflected here too.", "Mainframe.cs", "Start with Windows"),
            new Topic("Show on Discord", "show on discord|playing capri|discord status|discord activity",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Show on Discord controls the Playing Capri activity while Discord is running on this PC. It shows a short activity and elapsed time, not song titles or the contents of jobs.", "Mainframe.cs", "Show on Discord"),
            new Topic("Use her cursor", "use her cursor|use your cursor|your pink pointer|your cursor setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security > Use her cursor, beside Use your mouse and keyboard for jobs, lets YouTube searches, Apple Music and Spotify's volume slider use her visible pointer when a brain and the mouse permission are available. Spotify music uses play_music directly with either setting. Off uses the quick tools instead; it does not turn off explicit mouse and keyboard jobs.", "Mainframe.cs", "Use her cursor"),
            new Topic("Obsidian vault", "memory vault|obsidian|my vault|in obsidian|to obsidian|obsidian vault",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Obsidian vault lets you pick one of your Obsidian vaults, or Browse to any .md note. Her notes about you, me.md, then live in a Capri Memories note there, so you can read and edit them in Obsidian. Her transcripts and memories.md stay in her own folder. Pick Her own notes to put her back on me.md, and what she learned in the vault comes back with her.", "Mainframe.cs", "Obsidian vault"),
            new Topic("Her GIFs", "her gifs|your gifs|my gifs|gif shelf|add gifs|add a gif|add my gifs|send gifs|send a gif|send me a gif|saved gifs|save gifs|gifs do you have|gif card",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Her GIFs holds GIFs you save for her to send. Add GIFs picks .gif files, each named after its file, and each one can be renamed or removed there. She sends one when you ask, by name or at random, and now and then on her own when it fits, like a joke, a reaction or a win, at most one every 45 seconds. It plays in a card beside her on your PC for a few seconds, and a click closes it. They're kept in a gifs folder in her data folder: up to " + GifShelf.Most + " GIFs, each under 8 MB and " + GifShelf.MostFrames + " frames. Windows only for now, and never from Capri Remote on your phone.", "Mainframe.cs", "Her GIFs"),
            new Topic("Remember our chats", "remember our chats|memories md|chat transcripts|open her memories|your memories",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Remember our chats keeps daily transcripts and folds older chats into memories.md on this PC. Open her memories opens HER MEMORY, where each thing she remembers can be edited or forgotten, with Undo and her chat logs by day, and Edit as text opens memories.md inside Mainframe; Save writes your changes and Discard + reload reads the saved file again. A note changed elsewhere must be reloaded before saving. Turning Remember our chats off stops writing, folding, searching and reading these memories without deleting them. With a cloud brain, relevant recalled text and chats being folded go to that selected brain as context.", "Mainframe.cs", "Remember our chats"),
            new Topic("Perch", "perch fps|perch frame rate|perch setting|your animation speed",
                "Perch, the frames per second while she sits on a window, is no longer in Settings: Power saver already lowers how often she draws. A Perch you saved earlier still applies, and it is 30 fps otherwise; ask her to set it, from 10 to 60 fps, with her settings tool. The sway takes the same time at each setting; above 30 fps she draws intermediate frames for smoother movement.", null, null),
            new Topic("Power saver", "power saver|power saving|save power|saving power|go easy on my pc|easier on my pc|lighter on my pc|use less cpu|less cpu|free voice in games|free voice take over|free voice takes over",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Power saver is Off, In games (the default) or Always. While a game or anything full screen is in front, she draws herself less often while she sits still, holds perfectly still over anything full screen until she moves or talks, watches a game's screen for her reactions half as often, runs her background checks less often and listens at a gentler pace, so she might take a moment longer to hear you. Docked in Gaming Mode, she lets go of her art after a minute so the game gets the memory back. Always does that all the time. Your own settings stay as you set them: Watch my screen keeps its timing, and Listen for Capri and Clip my games keep working. In games and Always also let her free voice take over from HD voice while a game or video is full screen, so the graphics card is freed; Off doesn't. Her built-in brain on your PC is still the heaviest part: with the free NVIDIA key (Mainframe > BRAIN > Free key) she thinks on NVIDIA's servers while you play.", "Mainframe.cs", "Power saver"),
            new Topic("Music app", "music app|your music app|which music app|music app setting|play on apple music|use apple music|apple music instead|play music on youtube",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Music app picks where she plays music when you don't name an app: Spotify (the default, which is YouTube when Spotify isn't installed), YouTube or Apple Music. Naming an app, like play it on Apple Music, still wins. For Apple Music she opens the Apple Music app and searches and presses play with her cursor; without her cursor she opens it for you to search. Pause, skip and what's playing work the same in every app.", "Mainframe.cs", "Music app"),
            new Topic("Keep PC awake for jobs", "keep pc awake|keep my pc awake|keep the pc awake|keep screen on|keep my screen on|keep the screen on|keep screen awake|keep awake for jobs|sleep during jobs|laptop lid",
                "She always keeps both the PC and screen awake while a job runs, waits for your answer or has an active watch_for, and there is no setting for it. Her eyes need the screen on to see. She releases the hold when no jobs or watches remain, or when she quits. It does not change Windows power settings or simulate input. A closed laptop lid still sleeps. Explore after is separate: exploring never wakes a sleeping screen and still stops after half an hour.", null, null),
            new Topic("Water", "water check in|water check ins|water setting|water reminder setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Water turns her water check-ins on or off, with a default gap of 60 minutes in the time menu beside it. She waits until she is free to say the line; Edit check-in lines changes its wording.", "Care.cs", "Water"),
            new Topic("Stretch", "stretch check in|stretch check ins|stretch setting|stretch reminder setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Stretch turns her stretch check-ins on or off, with a time menu beside it and a default gap of 90 minutes. Edit check-in lines changes what she says.", "Care.cs", "Stretch"),
            new Topic("Look away", "look away setting|eye break setting|eye check ins|rest your eyes setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Look away enables check-ins to look away from the screen for 20 seconds. The time menu beside it sets the gap, which starts at 25 minutes; Edit check-in lines changes the words.", "Care.cs", "Look away"),
            new Topic("Sleep nudge", "sleep nudge|bedtime nudge|bedtime setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Sleep nudge gives one late-night check-in per night. The time menu beside it chooses the hour, with 1 am as the default; this is a nudge for you, separate from MOVES > Sleep for Capri's own nap.", "Care.cs", "Sleep nudge"),
            new Topic("Meals", "meals setting|meal check in|meal check ins|meal reminder setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Meals enables food check-ins if you've been at the PC since before noon. Mealtimes start at noon and repeat at the interval beside the switch, six hours by default; Edit check-in lines changes what she says.", "Care.cs", "Meals"),
            new Topic("Game break", "game break setting|game break check in|game break check ins",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Game break enables a check-in after time in a detected game, two hours by default. The time menu beside it changes that gap; changing games restarts the timer, and she waits until she is free and out of full-screen play before saying it.", "Care.cs", "Game break"),
            new Topic("Bored", "bored setting|bored check in|bored check ins|boredom check in|stop saying youre bored",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Bored controls her bored attention check-ins, starting at 60 minutes without attention in its time menu. Noticing her resets the wait and ignoring her makes later waits longer; Edit check-in lines includes Bored, Bored noticed and Bored ignored for those replies.", "Care.cs", "Bored"),
            new Topic("Edit check-in lines", "edit check in lines|check ins md|change check in lines|check in wording",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CAPRI > Check in on me > Edit check-in lines opens check-ins.md in Notepad, where you edit the bullets and save or remove all bullets under a heading to silence that check-in. Check in on me pauses all of them without changing their switches or times; Quiet or being busy postpones them, and more than ten minutes away resets their interval timers.", "Mainframe.cs", "Edit check-in lines"),
            new Topic("Comments", "your game comments|game commentary setting|comments setting",
                "Mainframe > Settings > GAMES > Comments selects Off, Events only or Chatty, separately from Watch my screen and Check in on me. Off stops game comments and live reactions, and it is the only game switch: she's on Events only until you pick another, and Gaming Mode, whether from its key, \"activate gaming mode\" or her settings tool, just flips Comments between Off and your last pick, saying so. Game comments use screen observations, sound levels and supported game logs, with Live reactions showing lines over the game instead of her bubble. Sound sensitivity, under Live reactions, decides whether big bursts of game sound count, and its Off ignores them.", "Mainframe.cs", "Comments"),
            new Topic("Live reactions", "live reactions|live reaction|reaction feed|reactions feed|hype lines|hype feed",
                "Mainframe > Settings > GAMES > Live reactions is on by default, right under Comments. It runs while her game comments do: Comments on Events only or Chatty, which it is by default, and never with Comments Off. When something happens in a full-screen game, like a kill, a death, a hit, a flash, a big sound while Sound sensitivity isn't Off, the screen changing or going dark, or a win or loss she can read on screen, her brain writes a short line that pops up on the right of the game's screen, a third of the way down, if it comes within about 2.5 seconds. A line that repeats one of her last ones is dropped, and with no brain or a slow one nothing shows. Up to four stack, newest at the bottom, and each fades after about 4 seconds. Her brain's look at what happened can follow, also within about 2.5 seconds. Each line sits on a dark plate in her Mainframe's look: quick lines read white beside a red bar, and her brain's look rose beside a cyan one. She says at most one out loud every 8 seconds, never over herself or you; her Quiet key keeps them as text, and so does ElevenLabs voice chat. The feed never takes clicks or focus and works over borderless full screen; exclusive full screen can't show it. Turned off, her game lines go back to her bubble.", "Mainframe.cs", "Live reactions"),
            new Topic("Sound sensitivity", "game sound sensitivity|sound sensitivity|game sounds sensitivity|game sounds|game sound|sounds in games|reacting to game sounds|react to game sounds|reacts to game sounds|reacting to sounds|react to sounds|game noise|headset turned down|ears ringing",
                "Mainframe > Settings > GAMES > Sound sensitivity, under Live reactions, runs from Off to 100% and is 100% by default; it is also her Game sounds setting. On, a big burst of your game's sound counts as a moment for her live reactions and game comments. Off, she ignores those bursts and still reacts to hits, deaths, kills, wins and losses she sees on screen or reads in a supported game's log; moving it off Off turns them back on. Her own loudness is VOICE > Volume, and her Quiet key keeps her reactions as text. She hears your game's level as Windows plays it, before your headset's own volume knob, so with Windows at 100% and your headset turned down every sound reads loud to her. Turn it down and a burst has to be louder and sharper before she reacts; Off ignores game sounds. Your game's volume stays as it is.", "Mainframe.cs", "Sound sensitivity"),
            new Topic("In full screen", "in full screen setting|hide in full screen|hide in fullscreen|disappear in fullscreen|hide over videos|mini player over full screen|mini player over fullscreen|player over games|music over fullscreen",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > In full screen picks what she does while the foreground window fills its monitor. Stay, the default, leaves her where she is and puts her mini player away. Keep player leaves her there and keeps her enabled mini player over borderless full-screen windows. Hide her hides her while the window fills its monitor and brings her back afterwards. Player only hides her the same way but keeps the mini player up. Windows cannot show the player over exclusive full screen. A manual hide stays hidden and Gaming Mode takes priority, putting the player away too. Speech and text follow her usual hidden behaviour.", "Mainframe.cs", "In full screen"),
            new Topic("Explore while I'm away", "explore while im away|explore while i'm away|afk exploring|scroll while away|explore my screen",
                "Explore while I'm away is off by default and set by Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Explore after, where any step but Off turns it on. After that long away, five minutes if you never picked one, she moves only her own pointer and scrolls a browser or reader page under your mouse. A YouTube page also works when Windows reports its matching video paused and no media in that browser is playing. She never clicks, types, opens or closes anything while exploring. Games, full-screen windows, password fields and blocked windows are excluded. Your mouse or keyboard input stops her; her own scrolling does not reset your away time. She stops after half an hour so your screen can turn off and your PC can sleep, and she never wakes a screen that has already gone off. With a brain that can see she sometimes makes one short comment using WATCH's pace.", null, null),
            new Topic("Explore after", "explore after|away time|afk time|exploring delay",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Explore after is Explore while I'm away's switch and its delay. Off, the default, keeps her from exploring; one, two, five, ten, fifteen or thirty minutes turn it on and set the idle time before she starts, with five minutes if you never picked one. Moving it back to Off keeps your last time for next time. Her own scrolling does not count as you coming back.", "Mainframe.cs", "Explore after"),
            new Topic("Gaming Mode", "gaming mode|game mode|gamer mode|gaming mod|game mod|gaming mood|your gaming hud|your game overlay|turn on the hud|activate the hud|enable the hud|start the hud|move the hud|move your hud|reset the hud|hud position|gaming mode key",
                "Say \"Hey Capri, activate gaming mode\" and she enters Gaming Mode. Gaming Mode has no switch of its own: it is Mainframe > Settings > GAMES > Comments. Anything but Off means Gaming Mode is on, so a game in front brings it up with nothing said. The default key is Ctrl + Alt + G; it, the phrase and her settings tool flip Comments between Off and your last pick (Events only if you've never picked), and she says so. Turning it off means Comments Off, which stays off until you turn it back on. She stays on your desktop as usual, you can still drag her, and she reacts when something happens in the game until it closes. Her HUD is switched off for now, so there's nothing to move. It works best on MAX INTELLIGENCE and is weaker on other brains. Settings > KEYS changes that key; press it again to turn the mode off, or ask turn off gaming mode. Gaming Mode does not by itself ask her to play. When she plays a game herself as a job, she goes into Gaming Mode by herself once the game is in front; it stays up until the game closes, and turning it off keeps it off for that job.", "Mainframe.cs", "Gaming Mode: Ctrl + Alt + G"),
            new Topic("Clip my games", "clip my games|clip my game|clip a game|game clips|saved clips|clips saved|your clips|clip that|scroll that bd|record my games",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Clip my games is off by default. When on, it keeps up to the last two minutes of a detected game's video and PC playback sound in memory while the game is in front. Say clip that or scroll that BD to use your default length, or name a length such as clip the last two minutes. CLIPS has a save-folder picker, default length from 15 seconds to 2 minutes, target frame rate from 15 to 60 fps, maximum resolution Auto/480p/720p/1080p and video bitrate Auto/2/4/8/12/20Mbps. Clips are MP4 files in your chosen folder, Videos\\Capri Clips by default. Folder changes affect future clips and do not move old files. FPS may drop under load or the 240 MB memory budget, especially in longer clips; Auto resolution may lower detail to stay smooth. Matching repeated requests within 8 seconds share one save and one notification. Each save chimes and pops up CLIP SAVED at the top right of the game's screen; click it to see the clip. Open clips folder in Settings > CLIPS opens them all.", "Mainframe.cs", "Clip my games"),
            new Topic("Save big moments", "save big moments|automatic clips|auto clips|automatic clipping|clip moments|big moments",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Save big moments is directly under Clip my games and off by default. Turning it on also turns Clip my games on; turning Clip my games off turns both off. With both on, her game commentary decides whether a moment is worth keeping and saves your chosen default length of buffered video and PC sound. Comments must be running: games run them unless you set Comments to Off, and with them Off she judges and saves nothing automatically. She reacts as usual, then saves it with no spoken notice; failures stay in her log. Moments under 30 seconds apart do not extend a clip or save another. Clips go to your chosen CLIPS folder (Videos\\Capri Clips by default) like any other clip and take up space the same way; there is no limit on how many she saves and she does not delete old clips.", "Mainframe.cs", "Save big moments"),
            new Topic("Default length", "default length|clip length|clip duration|recording duration",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Default length chooses 15, 30, 45, 60, 90 or 120 seconds for clip that and Save big moments. The default is 30 seconds. An explicit request such as clip the last two minutes overrides it, using only video already buffered.", "Mainframe.cs", "Default length"),
            new Topic("Frame rate", "frame rate|clip fps|recording fps|clip frame rate",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Frame rate targets 15, 24, 30 or 60 fps for future capture. 30 fps is the default. Slow capture or the 240 MB rolling memory budget can reduce the actual rate, especially for longer clips. It does not invent extra frames or change playback speed.", "Mainframe.cs", "Frame rate"),
            new Topic("Resolution", "clip resolution|recording resolution|clip quality|resolution",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Resolution chooses Auto or up to 480p, 720p or 1080p, preserving the game's shape without upscaling. Auto starts at up to 1080p and can lower it to stay smooth. New capture uses the chosen maximum; it cannot restore detail missing from older buffered frames.", "Mainframe.cs", "Resolution"),
            new Topic("Video bitrate", "video bitrate|clip bitrate|recording bitrate|bitrate",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Video bitrate chooses Auto or an H.264 average target of 2, 4, 8, 12 or 20 Mbps for future saves. Higher values make larger files. Auto uses the picture size, up to 12 Mbps; bitrate is not a guaranteed file-size or peak limit.", "Mainframe.cs", "Video bitrate"),
            new Topic("Save folder", "clip folder|clips folder|save folder|clip destination|where are clips saved|where are clips stored",
                "Mainframe > Settings > CLIPS > Choose folder picks an existing folder for future MP4s. Videos\\Capri Clips is the default. Existing clips stay where they were. Open clips folder opens the selected folder; clicking a CLIP SAVED popup reveals that particular file, including an older clip in its original folder.", "Mainframe.cs", "Save folder"),
            new Topic("Fast hands in games", "fast hands|haiku in games|games on haiku|play on haiku|why haiku|hands brain|cheaper games|faster in games",
                "Mainframe > Settings > Advanced Settings > BRAIN > Fast hands in games is on by default. On a Claude key, a job that plays a game runs on Claude Haiku 5.5, because a game doesn't wait: turns take about 3 seconds instead of 10 or more and cost a fraction. When she's stuck she asks the brain you picked what to do, or Claude Sonnet 5.5 if you picked Haiku, which costs a few cents a time. Chat stays on the brain you picked. Turn it off to play on your picked brain. Other brains aren't changed by it.", "Mainframe.cs", "Fast hands in games"),
            new Topic("Quick moves in games", "quick moves|quick moves in games|your combo tool|combo tool|key combos|anti cheat|anticheat|kernel anti cheat|battleye|riot vanguard",
                "In a game job she can send a quick run of key presses, holds and clicks in one go, with the timing she picks, then look once, so moves that need timing, like sprinting into a jump, land together. Esc or the game leaving the front stops it and lets go of every key, and keys like Win + R still ask first. She never does quick moves while kernel anti-cheat is running, like Riot Vanguard, Easy Anti-Cheat, BattlEye, FACEIT or ACE, since games that use it can ban for input that isn't yours. Riot Vanguard usually loads at startup on a PC with Valorant or League of Legends installed, and while it's loaded she doesn't use them in any game. There's no setting for it.", "Computer.cs", "combo"),
            new Topic("Mini games", "mini games|mini game|minigames|tic tac toe|tictactoe|connect four|connect 4|rock paper scissors|desktop boards",
                "Right-click her > Play, or Mainframe > Settings > GAMES > Play, opens a choice of Chess, Connect four, Tic-tac-toe and Rock, paper, scissors. You can also ask play tic-tac-toe, play connect four, play rock paper scissors or play chess, even without a brain connected. Click a move or tell her a square, column or hand. On the board, tic-tac-toe uses 1-9, connect four 1-7, and rock paper scissors R, P or S; arrows and Enter also work. N starts another round and Esc closes those boards. Chess uses mouse moves and its own buttons. Every board has easy, normal and hard levels, normal by default: add one when you ask, like play connect four on easy, click it on the board, or say switch to hard while a board is up. On tic-tac-toe, connect four and rock paper scissors, changing level starts a new round. Easy is beatable. Hard tic-tac-toe never loses. In rock paper scissors easy means she has a habit you can spot, normal is pure chance, and hard guesses from the hands you've already played, never the one you're playing now. Rock paper scissors is first to three points, and scores last for the session.", "Hands.cs", "mini_game"),
            new Topic("Game controls", "game controls|teach you controls|teach game controls|game instructions|your saved controls",
                "Mainframe > Settings > GAMES > Controls opens an editor for a game's controls. Use its window title as the name; the game open now is filled in for you. You can also say remember the controls for The Binding of Isaac: shoot with the arrow keys, or show my controls for The Binding of Isaac. They are saved in games/<game>.controls.md, separately from what she learns while playing, and every game job reads them before its first move. New instructions go below old ones; edit the file to replace controls.", "Hands.cs", "game_notes"),
            new Topic("Chess", "chess|chess board|chess difficulty",
                "Ask play chess, or play chess on easy, normal or hard. You have white unless you say I'll be black. Click a piece then a legal square, or drag it; promotion offers queen, rook, bishop and knight. Undo or take that back, new game, hint and resign work by text, voice or the board buttons. Levels change on the board. Her native engine and stock reactions need no brain or key; speech uses her installed local voice. Scores last for the session. Closing discards the position without asking. Requests for chess.com stay in the browser.", "ChessBoard.cs", "CHESS"),
            new Topic("Drawing on your screen", "drawing on your screen|draw on my screen|draw on your screen|drawing on my screen|drawing on screen|your drawing|her drawing|your ink",
                "Ask her to draw and she does it in pink right on your screen: \"draw me a cat\", \"write hi on my screen\", \"circle the start button\", \"point at the save button\". For things already on screen she looks at the monitor you're using first. Clicks go straight through the ink. It stays until you say \"clear your drawing\", \"remove it\" or \"get rid of that\", hold Esc, pick Clear her drawing from her menu, or ask for a new drawing. Say \"add\" to keep what's there.", null, null),
            new Topic("Copy a reply", "copy a reply|copy your reply|copy her reply|copy what you said|copy your message|copy your text",
                "Right click her reply bubble to copy the whole reply, even the pages of a long one that aren't showing. The bubble then shows > sys: copied. A left click dismisses the bubble.", null, null),
            new Topic("Handing her a file", "handing her a file|hand you a file|give you a file|drop a file|drag a file|attach a file|read a file|read files|files can you read|files do you read|file types|file formats|read a pdf|read a spreadsheet",
                "Drag a file onto Capri, or ask read followed by its full path; quote a path with spaces. Mod and plug-in files dropped on their own go to Import mod instead, after she asks. She reads text and code files, Word .docx, Excel .xlsx, PDFs through Windows OCR, and PNG, JPG, JPEG, GIF, BMP and WebP pictures. Pictures use the selected brain when it can see, otherwise Windows OCR. Her selected brain answers from the contents, which stay available for a few follow-up turns; she reports unreadable files and any omitted contents.", "Hands.cs", "read_file"),
            new Topic("Finding files", "find files|find a folder|find game folders|finding files|file search",
                "Ask for a file or folder by its name or a plain description, like show me the path to the cyberpunk game folder. She searches names on a worker, in your personal folders and game locations first, and through your fixed drives if nothing turns up there. Results show full paths, closest match first. Say show it to me or open that folder to select the first in File Explorer; say stop to cancel a running search. That quick search reads names only; to look by words inside, kind or date, see Organising files.", "Hands.cs", "find_file"),
            new Topic("Organising files", "organise files|organize files|edit a file|write a file|read a file|sort my files|sort my downloads|tidy my files|tidy my downloads|make a folder|move files|rename a file|files from a date|search inside files|undo a move|file changes",
                "Ask in your own words with any brain: find the PDF that mentions my lease, show me videos from last week, what did I download today, or find photos from 2026-11. She looks through your Desktop, Downloads, Documents, Pictures, Videos, Music and the rest of your user folder and other drives for up to 8 seconds, reads the words inside text files, Word, Excel and PDF documents, and lists numbered results; she can't see inside videos, photos or music, so those match by name, kind and date. Then say move 1 and 3 into a folder called Beach, rename 2 to beach day, make a folder called Taxes in Documents, or sort my Downloads by kind, month or year. She can also read a file's words, write a new text file, or edit or add to a text file like notes.txt; she never writes over a file and won't touch apps or scripts. Moving, renaming, sorting, writing and editing ask first unless you're on Blackwall, with Allow and No keys on her bubble, never delete anything and skip system and app folders. Every file job shows in Workspace's Her files chat with an Undo key. Say undo that to put the last change back; her last 30 changes are kept in file-changes.json in her data folder.", "Hands.cs", "files"),
            new Topic("Website nicknames", "website nicknames|website aliases|remember a website|name a website",
                "Say remember this website as apples, call this site apples, or remember apples is example.com/page. She reads the front browser's address without moving input, or asks for the address if unavailable. Open apples, check out the apples website, go to apples and take me to apples open that whole nickname; in chrome chooses Chrome. What websites do you know lists them, and forget the apples website removes one. Nicknames are in websites.json next to memories.md in her data folder.", "Hands.cs", "website_nickname"),
            new Topic("Moves", "your moves|move you|move capri|ride cursor|hop off|sit here|hang here|sit on windows|bring here|bring to this screen",
                "Drag Capri to place her, double-click her to ride the cursor, or right-click > Move for Sit here, Hang here, Lie down, Ride cursor and monitor choices. Sit on windows, also a switch under MOVES in Mainframe's Advanced Settings, lets her land on window edges; Stand up releases a chosen seat and Hop off ends a cursor ride, also available with Ctrl + Alt + C. Mainframe > CAPRI has Bring here and Hide Capri, and double-clicking her tray icon brings her back.", "Mainframe.cs", "Sit on windows"),
            new Topic("Hide Capri", "hide capri button|show capri button",
                "Mainframe > CAPRI > Hide Capri hides her and stops her movement, cursor riding, chat and speech. The button changes to Show Capri to bring her back. Hiding her keeps Capri running.", "Mainframe.cs", "Hide Capri"),
            new Topic("Bring here", "bring here button|bring capri here button",
                "Mainframe > CAPRI > Bring here wakes her, ends a cursor ride and clears her seat. She appears near the lower-right corner of the monitor containing your cursor.", "Mainframe.cs", "Bring here"),
            new Topic("Ride cursor", "ride cursor button|hop off button",
                "Mainframe > CAPRI > Ride cursor makes her follow your mouse smoothly on its monitor. Mouse clicks pass through her while she rides. The button becomes Hop off; stopping the ride returns her to her previous position.", "Mainframe.cs", "Ride cursor"),
            new Topic("Notes", "me md|your notes|her notes|open her notes|edit your notes|remember things about me",
                "Mainframe > Settings > YOU > Open her notes edits me.md inside Mainframe, or her existing note in your Obsidian vault. Save writes your changes; Discard + reload reads the saved file again. If she or another app changed the file, reload it before saving. Tell her remember or forget a fact, or edit the file and save it; she reads these notes when you chat. Get to know me writes your nickname, pronouns and interests there too.", "Mainframe.cs", "Open her notes"),
            new Topic("File editor", "file editor|edit your files|edit her files|edit your file|your text files|her text files",
