            new Topic("personality.md", "personality md|edit your personality|change your personality|personality file",
                "Mainframe > Settings > YOU > Her personality > Edit personality.md opens personality.md in Notepad, starting from her default. Rewrite how she acts and talks, save, and her next reply uses it. Her safety lines stay in her code and always come after it, so it can't change them. Reset to her default puts her back and keeps yours as personality.backup.md. On Mac and Linux it's under Settings in her right-click menu.", "Mainframe.cs", "Edit personality.md"),
            new Topic("Reminders", "your reminders|set a reminder|set reminders|reminder setting|do you have reminders|can you set reminders|can you remind me later|can you remind me tomorrow|how do reminders work|can you set a timer|can you set timers|do you have timers|do you have a timer|how do timers work",
                "Ask remind me in 20 minutes to take the pizza out, remind me in 3 days to water the plants, or remind me on 5 December at 9am to call Mum. Dates accept YYYY-MM-DD, day then month, or month then day, with an optional year for named months. No year means the next occurrence; no time means 9am. A date with an explicit year must be in the future. She uses your PC's local clock and saves reminders in reminders.json. Ask list my reminders or cancel the pizza reminder to manage them. Timers are reminders too: set a timer for 10 minutes, and cancel my timer stops it. Capri needs to be running to deliver them; reminders overdue when she starts are announced as late. Quiet and full-screen mode show reminders without speaking.", "Hands.cs", "remind"),
            new Topic("Stopwatch", "your stopwatch|a stopwatch|the stopwatch|stopwatch setting|do you have a stopwatch|can you run a stopwatch|how does the stopwatch work|how does your stopwatch work",
                "Ask start a stopwatch, check the stopwatch or how long has it been, and stop the stopwatch for its final time. There's one stopwatch, with no laps, and asking to start it while it runs says how long it's been. It isn't saved, so it ends when Capri closes.", "Hands.cs", "stopwatch"),
            new Topic("Screen watches", "watch for something|watch something for me|your screen watches|how do screen watches work|can you keep an eye on",
                "Ask tell me when my health is low, let me know when the download finishes, warn me if the boss spawns, or tell me when someone messages me. With a brain that can see, watch_for checks the visible screen about every three seconds, more slowly if the brain takes longer. Unchanged screens get another look at least every 30 seconds. She stays quiet until a match, waits while either of you speaks, and can warn you aloud in full-screen games. Hushed and Quiet keep alerts as text. Watches fire once by default; every_time waits for a clear look before another alert. Ask what are you watching for or stop watching, optionally naming one. Watches are not saved and end when she closes. Clock-based requests use remind.", "Lookout.cs", "watch_for"),
            new Topic("Routines", "your routines|saved routines|routine setting|save a routine|set up a routine|how do routines work|routine phrases",
                "Tell her when I say focus time, open Notepad to save a routine. Saving keeps the steps for later; saying focus time runs them like an ordinary request. Ask list my routines to see them or forget the focus time routine to remove one. They are saved on this PC in routines.json.", "Hands.cs", "routine"),
            new Topic("Stop a job", "stop a job|stop your job|stop you working|cancel a job|cancel your job|escape key|esc key|stop your task",
                "Press Esc while a mouse and keyboard job is running to stop it. Moving your own mouse does not cancel the job; Quiet controls unsolicited chatter separately.", "Capri.cs", "Esc"),
            new Topic("Her glow", "pink glow|cyan glow|glow round my screen|glow around my screen|glow round the screen|glow around the screen|border round my screen|border around my screen|using your mouse|who moved my mouse|mouse moved by itself|mouse moving by itself|mouse moves by itself|esc stops her",
                "While she moves your mouse or presses your keys, however briefly, a thin pink and cyan glow goes round the screen she's working on, with Capri's using your mouse. Esc stops her. on a badge just above the bottom. It's up for jobs on any brain, her shortcuts and media keys, games, Explore while you're away and her clones grabbing your cursor, and it goes the moment she gives control back. It shows even while she's hidden, so if your mouse moves with no glow, it wasn't her. Clicks go straight through it, and it stays out of screenshots and recordings. Press Esc to stop her.", "Hands.cs", "Capri's using your mouse. Esc stops her."),
            new Topic("Updates", "your updates|update you|update capri|check for updates|restart to update|your version",
                Packaged.Is ? "The Microsoft Store updates her once Microsoft has checked each release, so her own updater stays off. Settings and notes stay in her data folder across updates." : "Mainframe > CAPRI > Check for updates, or right-click > Help > Check for updates, checks for a newer version. She also checks automatically after startup and every three hours, downloads an available update and offers Restart to update. Settings and notes stay in her data folder across updates.", "Mainframe.cs", "Check for updates"),
            new Topic("Data folder", "your data|her data|data folder|where are your files|where do you store|localappdata|settings json|chat json",
                "On Windows her data lives in " + (Packaged.Is ? Packaged.Home(Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.LocalApplicationData)) : "%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Capri") + "; paste that path in Win + R or File Explorer. It includes settings.json, chat.json, me.md, memories.md, transcripts, reminders.json, routines.json and check-ins.md, with local brain and voice downloads in subfolders. API keys in settings are encrypted for the Windows user.", "Capri.cs", "settings.json"),
            new Topic("Security", "security setting|security presets|custom preset|your permissions|her permissions|blackwall|lockdown|guarded|trusted|bypass all permissions|why do you ask permission",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security opens SECURITY: Lockdown turns every action toggle off, Guarded turns the first three on, and Trusted, the default, turns the first seven on. Blackwall turns its usual eleven on, including passwords; friend requests stay off in every preset. Keep personal details out of her memories, under HER MEMORY, is on in every preset but Blackwall. Use tools your mods added, under HER MODS, is on in Trusted and Blackwall. A different mix shows Custom, and choosing a preset resets its toggles. With an action toggle off she asks first, except passwords and card numbers are yours to type and she asks first for the rest.", "Mainframe.cs", "SECURITY >"),
            new Topic("Browser choice", "choose a browser|which browser|browser choice|named browser|open websites",
                "Name Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Opera, Opera GX, Brave or Vivaldi to open a site or search there, for example open YouTube in Chrome. Otherwise she uses your default browser. If the named browser isn't installed she uses the default and says so. She opens a new tab in the named browser and brings it forward, and tells you if its window stays behind or hasn't appeared yet.", "Hands.cs", "open_website"),
            new Topic("Open apps, games and sites", "opening apps permission|open apps games and sites",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security > Open apps, games and sites controls opening things you request. On she opens them directly; off she asks first and does it after a yes.", "Hands.cs", "Open apps, games and sites"),
            new Topic("App volume", "app volume|volume mixer|volume of one app|one app louder|one app quieter|turn one app down|turn discord down|turn discord up|turn spotify down|turn chrome down|mute chrome",
                "With a cloud brain she changes one app's own volume in Windows' volume mixer when you ask, apart from your PC's volume: turn the game down, set Discord to 50%, mute Chrome, or ask what's making noise. She says where it ended up. An app shows in the mixer once it has made sound. Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security > Music, media and volume covers it. Windows only.", "Hands.cs", "app_volume"),
            new Topic("How your PC is doing", "whats using my cpu|what is using my cpu|whats using my memory|whats using my ram|why is my pc slow|why is my pc lagging|why is my computer slow|check my pc|how is my pc doing|how much ram|how much memory|how much disk space|how much space is left|pc performance|is my internet down|is my wifi down|whats my ping|check my internet|check my connection|is my internet slow",
                "With a cloud brain, ask what's using your CPU, why your PC is slow or how much space is left: she checks how busy the processor and memory are, which apps use the most, each drive's free space and a laptop's battery, then tells you. Ask is my internet down or what's my ping and she checks your connection: Ethernet or Wi-Fi, a few pings and whether sites look up. She only reads them and changes nothing. Windows only.", "Hands.cs", "pc_status"),
            new Topic("Music, media and volume", "music media and volume|media permission",
                "Mainframe > Settings > HABITS > Security > Music, media and volume covers playing media, adjusting PC volume and one app's own volume. On she does it when asked; off she asks first.", "Hands.cs", "Music, media and volume"),
